
find /home/user -name "myfile.txt"    --> Find a file by name (case-sensitive)


find / -iname "myfile.txt"   -->  Find a file by name (case-insensitive)


find . -type f -name "*.log"  --> Only find regular files (not directories)


find . -user viswa    --> to search based on user


find . -group flm     --> to search based on group


find . -perm 777    --> to search based on permissions


find / -type f -size +100M   --> Find files by size (e.g., larger than 100 MB)


find /path/to/search -type f -mtime -7    --> Find files modified within last 7 days


find . -type f -exec grep -l "search_string" {} \;   --> Combine find with grep to search file contents

explanation:
============
find .
   ↓
Find everything under current directory
   ↓
-type f
   ↓
Keep only regular files
   ↓
-exec
   ↓
Run grep on each file
   ↓
grep -l "viswa"   --> -l Only print the filename, not the matching line.
   ↓
Print only files containing "viswa"
